        "detail": "## Summary\n\n**Task:** Implement '?' keyboard shortcut on play screen to open help modal\n\n**Files changed (commit `edc746d`):**\n\n1. **`app/routes/play.tsx`** — Added `showHowToPlay` state, `toggleHowToPlay` callback, and a `useEffect` keyboard listener for `?` key that:\n   - Toggles the HowToPlayModal open/closed\n   - Skips when focus is on INPUT or TEXTAREA elements\n   - Cleans up listener on unmount (no memory leak)\n   - Uses `e.preventDefault()` to avoid interfering with other handlers\n   - Imported `HowToPlayModal` from components barrel, updated import budget comment\n   - Conditional render of `<HowToPlayModal onClose={...} />` alongside the existing LevelComplete modal\n   - Passed `onHelp={toggleHowToPlay}` to GameHUD\n\n2. **`app/components/GameHUD.tsx`** — Added optional `onHelp?: () => void` prop and a visible '?' button rendered next to the back arrow when `onHelp` is provided. Styled consistently with the existing back button (same size, rounded-xl, bg-white/70). Has `aria-label=\"How to play\"` for accessibility.\n\n**Acceptance criteria met:**\n- ✅ Pressing '?' opens HowToPlayModal\n- ✅ Pressing '?' again closes it (toggle via state)\n- ✅ Escape also closes (handled by HowToPlayModal's existing Escape listener)\n- ✅ Listener skips INPUT/TEXTAREA focus\n- ✅ Listener removed on unmount\n- ✅ Visible '?' button in GameHUD for mobile discoverability\n- ✅ No interference with canvas/game-board handling (document-level listener, e.preventDefault)\n\n**Validation:** typecheck ✅, lint ✅ (only pre-existing warning), tests ✅ (153/153 pass)"
